ulding county school district  meeting tuesday some cast doubt that the  coronavirus would affect their kids  those studies indicate children can be  infected  one teacher was not amused i had  students  making fun of the fact that i choose to  wear a mask  that's unacceptable back in elizabeth  new jersey politano says the priority is  giving students a quality experience  at home but their children are entitled  to equitable education and we're going  to work like hell to see that they get  them  in addition to their educational needs  more than 75 percent of students in  elizabeth public schools  qualify for free or reduced lunches the  district will continue their grab-and-go  plan to serve those meals to students  and every student will receive a device  and anthony just one more note that  first grade teacher we talked to she  told us  it's not just about the health concerns  but in terms of the social distancing  guidelines  she doesn't know how she could comfort a  first grader if they started to cry  on the first day of school that's a  challenge meg it really is thank you  very much
 

